      "problem": "If $A$ is a $9 \\times 11$ matrix that has $9$ pivot columns, then what is $\\textrm{dim(Null}(A))?$",
      "worked_solution": "We know that $\\textrm{dim(Null}(A))$ is the number of non-pivot columns in $A$. \n\nSince $A$ has $11$ columns and $9$ of them are pivots, then the number of non-pivot columns in $A$ is \n\n$$\n11-9=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\textrm{dim(Null}(A))=2$.",
